t(19, 960, """"At the end of my Ummah the Mahdi will come forth; Allah will give him rain to drink, the earth will bring forth its plants, he will give out wealth in fair measure, livestock will multiply and the Ummah will become great"

"My Ummah will enjoy, in the time of the Mahdi, a blessing the like of which it has never enjoyed: the sky will send abundant rain upon them, the earth will not withhold any of its plants, and wealth will be heaped up. A man will stand and say: O Mahdi, give me; and he will say: Take" """)

h(19, 1600, """Green pastures and meadows, not desert!""")

t(19, 2235, """Allah Almighty willing, by His might and His will

Even if the rain of mercy (ghayth) is abundant, it is completely different from "the rain of punishment" or "destructive floods", for several scientific and geographical reasons:

1. The rain of mercy comes down in "measure" and by divine distribution:
In the Noble Qur'an, the rain of mercy is always linked with mercy and fitting measure, as in His saying: "And it is He who sends down the rain after they had despaired, and spreads His mercy".

Physically, this means the rain of mercy comes down as successive drops that the earth has room for""")

t(20, 60, """and absorbs gently, not all at once like a waterskin bursting open suddenly to sweep everything away.

2. Washing the soil and feeding the depths:
On the surface of barren soil, after years of drought, harmful salts build up that stop crops from growing. Very light drizzle may not have enough force to wash these salts downward.

The rain of mercy has the ideal amount of water flowing calmly to enter the pores of the earth, so it gives the soil a "natural wash" and carries the harmful salts with it to the lower layers far from plant roots, which purifies the soil and readies it to sprout at once.

3. "The stirring and swelling of the earth" (plant swelling):
The Noble Qur'an describes with utmost precision what happens to the soil because of rain in His saying: "But when We send down water upon it, it stirs and swells and grows every kind of beautiful pair". It stirs and swells scientifically: dry soil contains empty pores and compressed clay layers. When the rain comes down, water molecules enter between the particles of earth, and the soil stirs and swells upward (rises) through absorbing the water. This "stirring and swelling" opens channels of air and oxygen for the seeds without the need to dig or plough it by human hand.

4. Stimulating hidden seeds:
The rain of mercy has enough water to dissolve the hard coat of the ancient desert seeds sleeping deep in barren desert ground. As soon as it touches them, the vital processes inside the seed begin and it makes its way toward the surface, and the new roots turn into a cohesive natural network that holds the soil and prevents its erosion in the future.""")

h(20, 1350, """The reason the Middle East will turn into a green Europe""")

t(20, 1955, """From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: "Soon the best wealth of a Muslim will be sheep he follows to the mountain peaks and the places where rain falls, fleeing with his religion from the fitnahs" (narrated by al-Bukhari).

The word "mountain peaks" means their tops and heights, and it carries the meaning of getting away, and away, and away, and away!

And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "The best of people in the fitnahs is a man holding the reins of his horse ... or a man withdrawn in his desert, fulfilling the right of Allah Almighty upon him" (Sahih al-Jami').

Why did the Prophet ﷺ praise what they did? And why did he describe their state as the best state in a time of fitnah that is widespread and overwhelming?

Because these people left the Matrix! They lived a world and a life other than our world and our life!

They left the system of:
🔴 Global education""")

t(21, 60, """🔴 The global economy
🔴 Global culture and media
🔴 Global medicine
🔴 Global worship
🔴 The integrated global dependency to which 99.9% of city dwellers submit, and the people of villages bordering the cities, or the people of villages that have become cities while their people think they are villages!""")

h(21, 650, """Why did the Prophet ﷺ praise them?""")

t(21, 1345, """The sign of the Smoke, and Allah knows best, comes after the Great Malhama and shortly before the appearance of the Dajjal; and Allah, our Great Lord above us, knows best and is Higher, Greater and more Majestic.

The sign of the Smoke is the hidden thing kept for the Dajjal, which the Dajjal knew very early, and he declared that he knew it by using the body of Ibn Sayyad to speak to the Prophet ﷺ from afar, because he feared to appear in his full flesh before the Prophet ﷺ. It, that is the sign of the Smoke, is the sign of his coming out and the cause of his anger, and it is what leads to the earth becoming harvested as if it had not flourished yesterday; that is, as if its people had not flourished with anything yesterday, as grief and regret for all who spent their wealth and lives making what they make to dominate the people of truth, so their industries are destroyed utterly. "As if it had not flourished yesterday" does not mean the earth as a creature that by its nature is not affected by what humans do and do not do on it, the earth of land, seas, rivers, mountains and straits; "as if it had not flourished yesterday" means as if its people had done nothing on it, so they return on it to their first ways: filling water from the well, building houses of mud and straw, riding animals for transport, and so on. So is the Great Malhama waged through this kind and form of life?
The answer is: no.

Modern, contemporary words came in narrations of weak chains narrated 1400 years ago, mentioning the word meteors in the war of the Great Malhama, in the word (their meteors), while at that time the Arab did not even know the primitive catapult. So who told the narrators of the hadiths that spoke about the Great Malhama about what is in the pictures attached to this post (rockets in the sky)? Who, 1400 years ago, told the narrators of the weak-chained hadiths about the pictures of rockets I attached to the post?""")

h(21, 2350, """The sign of the Smoke: between truth and illusion""")

t(22, 655, """Their being the greatest share of those sent to the Fire does not mean they are, for example, 100 billion people, because we must grasp the vast difference in the numbers of humans over 7000 or 10000 years, when there was no medicine and infant deaths were in very large numbers; a newborn who dies is not even accountable to enter Paradise or Hell; and many nations died upon Tawhid. Whenever we say nations, most likely today's person thinks we are talking about millions of humans! People imagine, for example, that Pharaonic Egypt's population was in the hundreds of thousands, or that the kingdom of Babylon and Assyria, Bilqis, and the kingdoms of Europe, China and India had, in today's person's imagining, enormous numbers of humans, and this is an imagining without evidence. Even when past nations lined up for battle, no one can prove their armies numbered in thousands .. The Western colonialist killed 20 million who were the inhabitants of North America, a number that resulted from human civilisations in the region thousands of years old; so after thousands of years they had become 20 million. So the fact must not be overlooked that the human population today is an unprecedented exceptional case in human history .. So a billion and a half people, on the scale of human numbers since Adam (peace be upon him), may .. and I say may .. represent a large part of the adults who will face the reckoning on the Day of Resurrection. As for births in human history, billions of children may have died at birth or after it, or even before reaching puberty and becoming accountable with Paradise and Hell on the Day of Resurrection .. because man, across his various ages, faced different nature and very many existential dangers .. insects .. animals .. diseases .. weather swings .. raids of people on each other .. regular wars .. drowning .. earthquakes .. and much else .. So a billion and a half today in the matter of Gog and Magog is a very frightening number compared with the numbers of those who lived before all ages. And Allah Almighty, our Lord above us, is Higher, more Knowing, Greater and more Majestic.""")

h(22, 1750, """Gog and Magog: not under the earth, two different components, not necessarily one race - many myths have been narrated about them""")

