t(24, 610, """Except the ruqyah of those who seek ruqyah for an affliction of touch (by jinn); in that there is the ruling of necessity.

As for anything else, I noticed a comment from one of the noble, virtuous brothers saying that it is not permissible at all, absolutely, for a Muslim woman to seek counsel even from behind a screen from any man whoever he is. This is a mistaken statement that calls for guidance and correction. As for most of those consulted being untrustworthy, yes, this is not a mistaken statement; but the generalisation is a mistake, because there are dozens of social issues that are "not women's issues" but ((social)), meaning ((family)) issues, falling under the knowledge of the rights of man and woman as Muslim spouses. These issues are not understood well even by the most capable Muslim women counsellors, who overlook aspects of them; how many of them misled a wife, and misled a husband, through lack of wisdom in them! Indeed we have seen men who are specialists and holders of doctorates who do not have the right understanding of life and of solving family issues in a wise and sound way; so what do you think of women ruled by emotion, who do not see clear aspects at the moment they give counsel to a woman? We have seen with our own eyes famous ones among them saying what no Shariah would accept when its understanding of clear verses in the Book of Allah Almighty is made the judge!

So the principle is that a Muslim woman seeking a ruling from a man of knowledge, understanding and wisdom is one of the foundations of reform on earth, and not impermissible as our brother said. What is impermissible is that the one asked for a ruling and counsel is not "of confirmed righteousness", one whose righteousness, chastity, religion and trustworthiness people are sure of through their experience of him, not through his own words. Without this condition it is forbidden for a Muslim woman to seek counsel from a man.""")

h(24, 1750, """A Muslim woman should seek counsel only from one whose trustworthiness and righteousness people have tested, and from behind a screen!""")

t(24, 2330, """Hundreds, not merely dozens, of brothers, men and women, the men ((far more in number)), contacted me through this channel over 4 years seeking counsel on issues in their lives. But here I address a word to no more than 5% of our sisters who contacted me during the four years seeking advice and counsel. It is my duty, and I do not count it a favour to them or to anyone; rather it is my duty toward every Muslim man and woman. But an issue is presented once, and I am used to hearing an issue only once; logic and reason say that an issue is presented once, and logic says I should give the advice only once. But it befits neither reason, nor wisdom, nor manners that the same issue be presented to me 500 times with the same words of grievance in it,""")

t(25, 85, """with the very same words explaining what happened to the person as a wronged one, and that this be presented to me for years. And out of embarrassment, manners, modesty and decency I carry the load and bear the weight of this repetition that has no logic to it, and I keep saying: perhaps the matter will stop.""")

h(25, 620, """A word to some of our sisters: counsel when it repeats itself!""")

t(25, 1240, """Everyone who has begun using this means of contact without wisdom, reason or logic will be blocked. This door is open to answer a religious, or humane-religious, enquiry: a word and its reply. But the matter has often turned into loading me with burdens that have nothing to do with me! This door was not opened for me to share anyone's worries! It is not reasonable that worries be complained to me daily, nor reasonable to tell me ((hundreds)) of issues and details I am not responsible for in the lives of a number of individuals who have suffered for long years.

It is not my role to be a psychiatrist who listens daily to dozens of details of worries from several people about the details of what happened to them over the course of their lives, of which I was never part for even a day, so that I bear a thousand stories upon stories from every person and hundreds of details: we went, we said, we did, 10 years ago we did, and last week so-and-so said such and such. All these people I deal with in full patience; among them are some whose this-thing I have borne for four years, some for a year and a half, some for two years, and I bear, reply and console; but all this has become exhausting and cannot be borne any longer, not even for a minute!

Even if work like this were done for money, I would not do it, even for billions, not even millions. All my contact since I opened this channel is for the sake of Allah Almighty, and I will not answer anyone for money, as I have never done before.

Anyone who cannot keep himself from this harm is asked to leave my account wisely, and I wish him success; but no one can bear more than this. The matter has become the cause of great exhaustion, and I hope I am not forced to block, because I will not be patient with this exhaustion any more than this.""")

h(25, 2250, """Will the stop to replying on WhatsApp begin? Charitable work turned into a door to harm!""")

